        "answerEnglish": "Inclusion of persons with disabilities requires accessible education, employment, transport, digital services and public infrastructure. Accessibility standards, assistive technologies, inclusive education and skill development can expand opportunities. Easy access to social security and government services is also important. Public awareness is needed to reduce discrimination and negative stereotypes. Genuine inclusion requires treating persons with disabilities as equal rights-bearing citizens rather than merely as recipients of welfare."
