        "answerEnglish": "Administrative accountability is supported by parliamentary oversight, judicial review, the Right to Information, institutions such as Lokpal, audit reports, social audits and internal administrative controls. Grievance-redress mechanisms also provide citizens with a means to challenge poor administration. Digital records and transparent procedures can improve monitoring. The effectiveness of these mechanisms depends on institutional independence, adequate resources, transparency and timely action."
